# Environment Variables — DeepTrics

Copy this file to `.env` (and `.env.local` for local overrides) and fill in the
values that apply. Vite exposes any variable prefixed with `VITE_` to the app via
`import.meta.env`.

```bash
# ── Contact ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shown across the site (phone / email / WhatsApp CTA).
VITE_CONTACT_PHONE=+91 00000 00000
VITE_CONTACT_EMAIL=hello@deeptrics.com

# WhatsApp number in international format WITHOUT "+" or spaces.
# Example: 919876543210  →  results in https://wa.me/919876543210
VITE_WHATSAPP_NUMBER=919876543210

# ── Enquiry form ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The URL the enquiry form POSTs JSON to (your form backend, CRM, or an
# email/automation service such as Formspree, Basin, Getform, Zapier webhook).
#
# IMPORTANT: if this is left empty, the form will NOT pretend to succeed.
# It shows an honest "submission not configured" notice and offers WhatsApp /
# email instead.
#
# Example (Formspree):  https://formspree.io/f/yourFormId
# Example (Zapier):     https://hooks.zapier.com/hooks/catch/123456/abcdef/
VITE_ENQUIRY_ENDPOINT=
```

## What the form sends

A JSON POST with `Content-Type: application/json` and this shape:

```json
{
  "submittedAt": "2026-10-30T12:00:00.000Z",
  "name": "…",
  "phone": "…",
  "email": "…",
  "eventType": "…",
  "date": "…",
  "location": "…",
  "budget": "…",
  "details": "…"
}
```

The form treats any 2xx response as success; anything else shows an error state.
